# TEMPLATE CONFIGURATION

> **Phase 0 Reference** - Template-first approach

---

## TEMPLATE LOCATION

```
r-genie/01_Technical_Design_Agent/
├── templates/
│   ├── design-style.yaml           # Structure, naming, diagrams config
│   └── design-template-guide.md   # Content guide: what goes where, when to produce
└── examples/
    └── *.md                        # Example formats to match
```

---

## PRE-DESIGN CHECKLIST (MANDATORY)

Before generating ANY content:

- [ ] `templates/design-style.yaml` read (structure and inclusion rules)
- [ ] `templates/design-template-guide.md` read (content guidance: what goes where, when to produce)
- [ ] `examples/` folder read (all .md files for formatting reference)
- [ ] Matching example selected for project type
- [ ] Sections identified per template structure
- [ ] Diagram placements identified per template guide
- [ ] Mermaid diagrams planned (NOT ASCII)

**If ANY check fails → DO NOT PROCEED → Fix first**

---

## TEMPLATE STRUCTURE

```yaml
# design-style.yaml structure
structure:
  sections:           # Core sections with include: true/false
    - name: "..."
      include: true   # Generate this section
  
  supplementary:      # Optional sections for Phase 5
    - name: "..."
      include: true   # Offer in Phase 5 if user requests

# Diagram placement defined in design-template-guide.md
# Section names and numbers defined in template, not rules
```

---

## TEMPLATE-DRIVEN RULES

### Main Document (Phases 0-4)
Generate sections where `structure.sections[].include: true`

### Supplementary (Phase 5)
- READ `structure.supplementary`
- ONLY offer items where `include: true`
- NEVER show items where `include: false`
- If user says "all per template" → generate ALL enabled items

---

## PHASE 0 OUTPUT

```
📋 Template Configuration Loaded:
   ✅ Style: [Custom | Default]
   ✅ Sections: [X sections]
   ✅ Diagrams: 3 essential + [Y] optional
   ✅ Example: [selected file]
```

---

## NO CONFIGURATION?

If templates unconfigured or empty → Use default R-GENIE style automatically
